73: Cloudflare remains authoritative for provider state. World maps those facts but does not duplicate their lifecycle. HP5 tightened that statement physically: lifecycle/capability health are now consumed through provider-owned projections, and the World doctor no longer reads the Cloudflare control credential or calls the lifecycle API directly. The provider subtree passed its full CI as an independent Git root, while the World Python/wheel boundary passed with that subtree absent; co-location is operational, not semantic ownership.
74: 
75: ## Retained Host-facing responsibilities
76: 
77: - validate current capabilities and derive a condition digest;
78: - derive a deterministic provider request ID from one Host Dispatch;
79: - persist prepared intent before delivery;
80: - record transport uncertainty as UNKNOWN;
81: - reconstruct the original request after Host replacement;
82: - query, validate and map the original provider Receipt;
83: - map R2 Artifacts into Host `ArtifactRef` values;
84: - verify Browser screenshot, rendered HTML and Manifest as one generation-scoped bundle;
85: - preserve Task state and Ready Frontier while appending opaque extension facts;
86: - keep provider success separate from Host Verification and completion.
